"""Blind evaluation set v16 (Round F: configuration-realism measurement; NO reasoning change).

Why v16: Blind v15 (Round E) scored 59.3% / 38.5% critical miss and was run only under the legacy
default config (top_k_differential=5). Read-only analysis showed the 5-slot differential cap
interacting with all-zero turn-1 scores. The real competition runtime enables competition retrieval
(differential size 25). Two attempted code fixes (tie-break ordering; never splitting a tie) were
measured on development sets, found to regress or to violate documented prompt-size invariants, and
were reverted -- so the runtime is byte-identical to Blind v15's: FINAL_REASONING_SHA
659c7dc6cdb484dc7dc351a39c52eea71a5b621f. This fresh set exists to measure, honestly, how the SAME
frozen code behaves under BOTH configurations (declared in advance in the manifest, one run each):
  (a) default/legacy (comparable to v12-v15), (b) NOVA_COMPETITION_RETRIEVAL=1 (competition-like).
Blind v3-v15 are REFERENCE-ONLY.

Authoring rules (same discipline as every prior set):
  1. No sentence/phrase copied from any earlier blind/dev/held-out set (6-gram narrative-overlap
     scan, see manifest). Chief complaints deliberately span a REALISTIC range of specificity
     (some detailed, some lay/vague) -- v15 skewed vague by design; this set does not.
  2. Tier-1 targets use knowledge/diseases ids; Tier-2 use 'tier2:<id>' with scoring_expected=False;
     unknown/OOD use 'unknown' + scoring_expected=False.
  3. ground_truth frozen BEFORE the first run (blind_v16_manifest.json SHA-256).
Hand-authored synthetic vignettes, never real patient data.
"""

